# ORION non-negotiable rules

- Use `supabase.auth.getUser()` on the server, never `getSession()`. Re-check fresh database role and scope in every server action, route, middleware decision, and export.
- Never cache role in browser storage; use `router.push` for role-sensitive navigation and never `router.back()`.
- Select listed columns only, destructure `{ data, error }`, display errors, and use try/catch/finally.
- Money: integer pesewas in TypeScript, `numeric(12,2)` in Postgres, all calculation through `lib/money.ts`.
- Zod validates server input; no SQL string interpolation; no `any`.
- Every table has RLS, every reporting view is `security_invoker`, and every status-changing database function is fixed-search-path `SECURITY DEFINER`.
- Never log member names or amounts or put member data in URLs/errors.
- Data pages are dynamic; services use Africa/Accra; PWA sign-out clears all Dexie/browser storage before hard navigation to `/login`.
